/-!
# Lean refutations of entry into 102 traps of the trap modules

In the game of 20 cells some node cannot reach each of 240 traps of the trap modules, so entry into each is false ([what
failed](../../negative-results/columns/missed-traps.md)). Here the kernel checks that refutation for 102 of them, 1 of
[WordTraps](WordTraps.md), 1 of [NineTraps](NineTraps.md), 7 of [TenTraps](TenTraps.md), 15 of
[ElevenTraps](ElevenTraps.md), 13 of [TwelveTraps](TwelveTraps.md), 13 of [ThirteenTraps](ThirteenTraps.md), 15 of
[FourteenTraps](FourteenTraps.md), 1 of [FarWalls](FarWalls.md), 7 of [CensusTraps13](CensusTraps13.md), 7 of
[CensusTraps14](CensusTraps14.md) and 22 of [CensusTraps15](CensusTraps15.md): for each, the closed set of windows that
`miss_tables` finds at the least width where some node of the game cannot reach the trap, 2 to 17 cells and 21 to 1,935
states, is closed and apart from the trap, and `not_absorption` of [MissedTraps](MissedTraps.md) refutes entry.

* `away_<trap>`, with `_closed` and `_apart`: the closed set apart from each trap.
* `<trap>_not_absorption`: some finitely supported right half driven by the trap's block never enters it.
* `refutedTraps`, `refutedTraps_not_absorption`: the list of the 102 traps and the refutation of entry into each.

The sets come from `python -m computations.lock_chain --lean-refuted`. The natural-language argument is
`RefutedTraps.md`, beside this file.
-/

@[expose] public section

-- Sequential elaboration: the kernel checks would otherwise run in parallel and stack their memory.
set_option Elab.async false

namespace Rule30Open

open Ruliology.CellularAutomata

/-- A closed set apart from `trap01` of WordTraps: windows of 16 cells, labels modulo 2, 1518 states. -/
def away_trap01 : WTrap :=
  { b := [false, true], K := 16, m := 2, n := 1518, lb := 1, ib := 11,
    u := 1,
    R := ,
    L := ,
    S :=  }

theorem away_trap01_closed : away_trap01.closedCheck = true := by decide +kernel

theorem away_trap01_apart : away_trap01.apart trap01 = true := by decide +kernel

/-- **Some finitely supported right half driven by `01` never enters `trap01`.** -/
theorem trap01_not_absorption : ¬ trap01.Absorption :=
  not_absorption _ away_trap01 away_trap01_closed rfl (by decide) away_trap01_apart (by decide)

